site of an old monastery, the oldest building in New Orleans west of downtown. Quality."},{"business_id":"zwe9H6Xxqb1_E09A20Ptgg","review_id":"N00XwnAGa_8Jk-xYUWkKHw","date":"2018-01-20T01:24:26","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9300848841667175,"text_excerpt":"Lively neighborhood crowd @ Le Citron. Best I can say now is that \"Bistro Le Citron\", long our neighborhood favorite, is back. The \"rude\" person has been gone for over a year now. When Chef Dave is in and open, place is just great, albeit with more limited menu choices. All of us long time patrons just LOVE Dave and his stuff. May GOD Bless Dave! We were there tonight. Dave is open, several nights/week, with \"Don\", his trusty waiter-bartender on duty. Offerings were smothered pork chops with mashed potatoes and black-eye peas, fried chicken platter, or those super Dave's char-broiled cheddar cheeseburgers. Call Chef Dave @ 504-566-9051 to see what his menu is for your night. BTW, The buil..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"zwe9H6Xxqb1_E09A20Ptgg","photo_id":"CWUHWNNTPw7n6KL3C-WKIQ","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/CWUHWNNTPw7n6KL3C-WKIQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9138273000717163},{"business_id":"zwe9H6Xxqb1_E09A20Ptgg","photo_id":"AYP1JPcHs4kx0F_7mtUl6w","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/AYP1JPcHs4kx0F_7mtUl6w.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.87714022397995},{"business_id":"zwe9H6Xxqb1_E09A20Ptgg","photo_id":"Uz3Bjc4ngKyuhy9qpoZCZg","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/Uz3Bjc4ngKyuhy9qpoZCZg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8126292824745178}]},"notebook_case":null}
